<title>UK: Natwest talks with Pru fail-FT.</title>
<headline>Natwest talks with Pru fail-FT.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Merger talks between National Westminster Bank and Prudential Corp collapsed last week, Saturday's Financial Times said.</p>
<p>The FT said the talks, which would have created a 27 billion pound ($45 billion) financial services company, failed after the companies were unable to agree on terms.</p>
<p>It said the talks were initiated by Prudential, but that the two sides never went into any detail about price or senior management.</p>
